{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> This sign was not given to Moses so that he would believe, for he had already been given the sign of the bush. Rather, He performed for him the sign that he should perform thus for the children of Israel, as it is written, 'so that they will believe' — the meaning is, you shall do thus for them. And He gave him [something] that was always with him, namely his staff, his support, as is the way of the elder, for like the way of a shepherd he did not come to Pharaoh."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:25.861092844Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}